{"w":2400,"h":3396,"lines":[{"x":0.088351342224742446,"h":0.015059596377351436,"w":0.05992282867431642,"y":0.031714387389674803,"t":"Test 1","c":1},{"w":0.3086419677734375,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1,"x":0.088477369920565541,"y":0.079799764541349627},{"h":0.018895348053517669,"c":1,"w":0.82921808878580727,"x":0.088477375254927895,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","y":0.11627907015686523},{"c":1,"t":"Passage 3 below.","w":0.17078189849853515,"y":0.1351590108238826,"x":0.088477363383555982,"h":0.016003780005537038},{"y":0.17432273271091259,"t":"The future of work","x":0.38888889475137839,"w":0.23868311564127603,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.8251028951009115,"x":0.088477358937902678,"y":0.21220930216651124,"t":"According to a leading business consultancy, 3-14% of the global workforce will need to switch","h":0.017472676590558955},{"w":0.77572016398111976,"y":0.22965116263126772,"h":0.017441860778592888,"t":"to a different occupation within the next 10-15 years, and all workers will need to adapt as","x":0.086419753298458579,"c":1},{"y":0.24558303933416525,"t":"their occupations evolve alongside increasingly capable machines. Automation - or 'embodied","w":0.81275721232096365,"h":0.018951843989611583,"c":1,"x":0.086419747724130025},{"x":0.086419748558173901,"w":0.80658437093098956,"y":0.26442873983227388,"t":"artificial intelligence' (AI) - is one aspect of the disruptive effects of technology on the labour","h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1},{"w":0.7408493550618489,"t":"market. 'Disembodied AI', like the algorithms running in our smartphones, is another.","h":0.020640340654532685,"x":0.08636507452500515,"c":1,"y":0.28175807577547074},{"x":0.086419755189597824,"y":0.31831395332843937,"t":"Dr Stella Pachidi from Cambridge Judge Business School believes that some of the most","w":0.7633744812011718,"c":1,"h":0.017441860778592888},{"c":1,"x":0.086326768859094419,"t":"fundamental changes are happening as a result of the 'algorithmication' of jobs that are dependent","y":0.33323542393222649,"w":0.84383056640624998,"h":0.022160562665779815},{"t":"on data rather than on production - the so-called knowledge economy. Algorithms are capable of","w":0.82933349609374984,"h":0.020119701875253138,"x":0.088427242730185096,"y":0.35311079247370747,"c":1},{"y":0.37209302309658399,"c":1,"t":"learning from data to undertake tasks that previously needed human judgement, such as reading","w":0.82098765055338541,"h":0.017482948527880904,"x":0.086419754875864591},{"x":0.086268353949219209,"t":"legal contracts, analysing medical scans and gathering market intelligence.","w":0.64222534179687496,"h":0.02363537113293035,"c":1,"y":0.38554426489980409},{"w":0.77383392333984358,"y":0.42148822705603717,"c":1,"h":0.021039825727015682,"x":0.088399717363984956,"t":"'In many cases, they can outperform humans,' says Pachidi. 'Organisations are attracted to"},{"w":0.79240397135416663,"h":0.02195678414388591,"c":1,"x":0.088363627543421988,"y":0.44007004420100504,"t":"using algorithms because they want to make choices based on what they consider is \"perfect"},{"h":0.02186621091952734,"w":0.57231918334960941,"x":0.086298398722902472,"y":0.45778455706379684,"c":1,"t":"information\", as well as to reduce costs and enhance productivity?"},{"y":0.49411071842668108,"x":0.086419745964897265,"t":"'But these enhancements are not without consequences,' says Pachidi. 'If routine cognitive tasks","w":0.82510289510091139,"h":0.017517188693384589,"c":1},{"x":0.088398824288291281,"w":0.80056833902994795,"t":"are taken over by AI, how do professions develop their future experts?' she asks. 'One way of","h":0.021292514598832968,"c":1,"y":0.50967482303160061},{"t":"learning about a job is \"legitimate peripheral participation\" - a novice stands next to experts and","x":0.086336251584242713,"h":0.020952602157323197,"y":0.52800794235167947,"w":0.82733652750651043,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"learns by observation. If this isn't happening, then you need to find new ways to learn.'","x":0.086311897052649911,"w":0.74716501871744789,"y":0.54646094920126831,"h":0.021151350580761452},{"h":0.018642614250048317,"c":1,"y":0.58309465180812425,"x":0.088400128400737119,"t":"Another issue is the extent to which the technology influences or even controls the workforce.","w":0.80466344197591155},{"c":1,"h":0.01751376490149259,"x":0.08847735848376051,"w":0.77366256713867188,"y":0.60174418587913803,"t":"For over two years, Pachidi monitored a telecommunications company. 'The way telecoms"},{"t":"salespeople work is through personal and frequent contact with clients, using the benefit of","x":0.088369738990267788,"y":0.61768917126299694,"w":0.78215586344401045,"h":0.021715346157761384,"c":1},{"t":"experience to assess a situation and reach a decision. However, the company had started using","x":0.088477370902530106,"h":0.017441860778592999,"y":0.63662790681671488,"w":0.80246912638346335,"c":1},{"y":0.65547703165536186,"t":"a[n] ... algorithm that defined when account managers should contact certain customers about","w":0.80864196777343744,"h":0.017488084777364743,"x":0.088477369948948503,"c":1},{"t":"which kinds of campaigns and what to offer them.'","w":0.43660100301106775,"c":1,"x":0.088314218305240791,"y":0.67143910453080891,"h":0.02042078213641163},{"w":0.80658437093098967,"x":0.088477361905179353,"y":0.70784883704671109,"h":0.017441860778592888,"c":1,"t":"The algorithm - usually built by external designers - often becomes the keeper of knowledge,"},{"c":1,"w":0.76762324015299499,"h":0.020376095361788304,"x":0.088408644321154861,"y":0.72491233023938828,"t":"she explains. In cases like this, Pachidi believes, a short-sighted view begins to creep into"},{"h":0.019856784312829001,"t":"working practices whereby workers learn through the 'algorithm's eyes' and become dependent","x":0.088424692333362601,"y":0.74195890197679604,"w":0.81698150634765632,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.81907816569010405,"x":0.0884047956462993,"y":0.76060085256251497,"t":"on its instructions. Alternative explorations - where experimentation and human instinct lead to","h":0.018520506868935249},{"t":"progress and new ideas - are effectively discouraged.","y":0.78052325566557423,"x":0.088477372773405616,"h":0.016002068109590928,"c":1,"w":0.45679011027018224},{"t":"Pachidi and colleagues even observed people developing strategies to make the algorithm work","x":0.08847737715399992,"y":0.81537102452351329,"h":0.017477812840042795,"c":1,"w":0.8168724060058592},{"y":0.83421672558335924,"x":0.088477375257591098,"w":0.82921808878580738,"c":1,"h":0.016195524146054185,"t":"to their own advantage. 'We are seeing cases where workers feed the algorithm with false data to"},{"t":"reach their targets,' she reports.","w":0.27160494486490883,"h":0.018967252176417371,"c":1,"y":0.85029069787731082,"x":0.088477363370014689},{"x":0.088477365995279944,"h":0.013081395583944722,"t":"24","c":1,"y":0.90697674401398698,"w":0.028806584676106792}]}